course: dictionary
lesson: 3120
title: Electrical: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Electrical means using electricity, or to do with electricity. Some words have more than one meaning, so the clues in the sentence tell you which one the writer wants. Ask yourself what the sentence is about.
explain: «A hot plug or socket, or a smell of burning, means an electrical fault.» Here electrical is about a problem in the wires or machines. An electrical fault is a fault with electricity, so the sentence tells you it is dangerous and a grown-up must be told.
explain: The second meaning is about people: «Dad is an electrical engineer» means he works with electricity. Words near electrical, like appliance, circuit, fault or engineer, are strong clues. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Electrical means using electricity or to do with electricity.
fact: An «electrical appliance» is a machine that runs on electricity, such as a kettle.
fact: An «electrical fault» is a problem with electric wires or equipment.
fact: An «electrical storm» is a storm with lightning.
fact: Never touch fallen power lines, and keep electrical things away from water.
exercise: «A hot plug or socket, or a smell of burning, means an electrical fault.» What is an electrical fault? | A cup of hot tea | A loud song on the radio | *A problem with electric wires or machines | A happy noise from the kitchen
exercise: «Water must never be used on an electrical fire, because water carries electricity.» What must you never use on an electrical fire? | *Water | Oxygen | Carbon dioxide extinguisher
exercise: «Dad is an electrical engineer.» What does electrical mean in this sentence? | Very shiny | Sad and slow | *Working with electricity | Made of plastic
test: «If a bath overflows, turn off the tap and keep away from electrical things.» What does electrical things mean here? | Things that float | *Things that use electricity | Things that are very old | Things made of wood
test: Which of these is an electrical storm? | A rainbow over the hills | *A storm with lightning | A quiet, dry afternoon
exam: Why is water leaking «onto electrical wiring» dangerous? | Water turns wires into plastic | Water makes wires shiny | *Water carries electricity and can cause harm | Wires need water to grow
